note: User ruling 2026-06-12 — left menu panel fully removed, functionality moved
to the macOS system menu bar. Software 3.0 compatible: Orb stays the first screen;
the menu bar is the quiet discoverability escape hatch (docs/02 §6), not primary nav.

DELIVERED (Workflow: 1 Sonnet implementer + 3 parallel adversarial lenses, ALL_GREEN):
- AppCommandBus.swift: 10 AppCommand cases, ObservableObject send/consume
  (pure, testable, last-intent-wins). Single source of truth for menu titles +
  shortcut keys (charter table test-asserted).
- TuringOSApp.swift: .commands with CommandMenu 项目(立项⌘N/连接仓库⌘O/项目总览⌘1) /
  视图(Orb主屏⌘0/内核调试面⌘D/Radar/Attention/CI) / 检查(CI检查⌘R/MorningRitual⌘M).
  WindowGroup remains FIRST scene (A1_10 lesson preserved); OrbView remains
  onboarded first screen; MenuBarExtra dot untouched.
- ContentView.swift: NavigationSplitView REMOVED (grep == 0 app-wide). NavItem
  enum + detail switch retained, full-frame; selection via pure nonisolated
  static applyCommand (tested without SwiftUI rendering).
- OrbView.swift: consumes intent commands by replaying the exact typed-intent
  path (vm.send(.inputSubmitted)); panel commands consumed by ContentView via
  @Published replay-on-subscription.
- 235 tests (+7 AppCommandBusTests), MIN_TESTS 228->235.

ARCHITECT-APPROVED DEVIATIONS (reviewed against card):
1. CommandGroup(replacing: .newItem) {} — REQUIRED: default File > New Window
   owns ⌘N (File menu matches key equivalents first); without this the
   chartered 立项 ⌘N is dead. Approved as functional enabler.
2. CJK-Latin spacing in menu titles ("Orb 主屏" vs card's "Orb主屏") — typography.
3. .connectRepo/.runCICheck land on the visible intent-suggestions escape hatch
   with precise TODOs naming GitConnect.detect(runner:) and
   IntentRouter.routeCIIntent(...) — honest visible deferral, future atom wires deep.

